{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class P851C {\n    private static final double EPS = 1e-9;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner();\n        int n = fs.nextInt();\n        if (n > 11) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        int[][] pts = new int[n][5];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = fs.nextInt();\n            }\n        }\n\n        List<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            boolean ok = true;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n && ok; j++) {\n                if (j == i) continue;\n                for (int k = j + 1; k < n && ok; k++) {\n                    if (k == i) continue;\n                    Vector u = new Vector(pts[i], pts[j]);\n                    Vector v = new Vector(pts[i], pts[k]);\n                    double cosTheta = u.dot(v) / (u.norm() * v.norm());\n                    if (Math.acos(cosTheta) < Math.PI / 2 - EPS) {\n                        ok = false;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (ok) ans.add(i + 1);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans.size());\n        ans.forEach(System.out::println);\n    }\n\n    static class Vector {\n        private final int[] vec;\n\n        Vector(int[] a, int[] b) {\n            vec = new int[5];\n            for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n                vec[i] = b[i] - a[i];\n            }\n        }\n\n        double norm() {\n            double sum = 0;\n            for (int x : vec) sum += (long) x * x;\n            return Math.sqrt(sum);\n        }\n\n        int dot(Vector other) {\n            int res = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n                res += vec[i] * other.vec[i];\n            }\n            return res;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class FastScanner {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n        String next() {\n            while (!st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\nimport io\n\nclass Vector:\n    def __init__(self, a, b):\n        self.vec = [b[i] - a[i] for i in range(5)]\n    \n    def norm(self):\n        sum_sq = sum(x * x for x in self.vec)\n        return math.sqrt(sum_sq)\n    \n    def dot(self, other):\n        return sum(self.vec[i] * other.vec[i] for i in range(5))\n\nclass FastScanner:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.br = sys.stdin\n        self.buffer = []\n        self.pos = 0\n    \n    def _fill_buffer(self):\n        while self.pos >= len(self.buffer):\n            line = self.br.readline()\n            if not line:\n                return False\n            self.buffer = line.split()\n            self.pos = 0\n        return True\n    \n    def next(self):\n        if not self._fill_buffer():\n            return None\n        token = self.buffer[self.pos]\n        self.pos += 1\n        return token\n    \n    def nextInt(self):\n        return int(self.next())\n\ndef main():\n    fs = FastScanner()\n    n = fs.nextInt()\n    if n > 11:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    pts = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(5):\n            row.append(fs.nextInt())\n        pts.append(row)\n    \n    ans = []\n    EPS = 1e-9\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        ok = True\n        for j in range(n):\n            if j == i:\n                continue\n            for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                if k == i:\n                    continue\n                u = Vector(pts[i], pts[j])\n                v = Vector(pts[i], pts[k])\n                norm_u = u.norm()\n                norm_v = v.norm()\n                if norm_u == 0 or norm_v == 0:\n                    continue\n                cosTheta = u.dot(v) / (norm_u * norm_v)\n                # Clamp cosTheta to [-1, 1] to avoid numerical issues\n                cosTheta = max(-1.0, min(1.0, cosTheta))\n                angle = math.acos(cosTheta)\n                if angle < math.pi / 2 - EPS:\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            if not ok:\n                break\n        if ok:\n            ans.append(i + 1)\n    \n    print(len(ans))\n    for a in ans:\n        print(a)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.067568756407127e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.062299427052494e-05, 